  "changes": [
    {
      "kind": "history",
      "description": "Retained the original header and Macintosh Plus modification history through November 2, 1985. Original comments remain exact where their operations survive. Later inline revision tags identify their surviving source context and do not date the ROM instructions. Comments about removed color, hierarchical, system-menu and help-menu paths were omitted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "menu_list",
      "description": "Restored the fixed 102-byte menu list: a six-byte header followed by sixteen six-byte entries. InitMList clears the list in place. InsertMenu measures the title in system font and plain face, adds thirteen pixels, shifts entries and adjusts their left coordinates. DeleteMenu shifts entries back and reduces lastRight. GetMenuBar and SetMenuBar copy the whole fixed list."
    },
    {
      "kind": "menu_bar",
      "description": "Restored CalcMBHeight as ascent plus descent plus five pixels. GetMenuInfo saves D4 and calls SetWPort and RestorePort around GetFontInfo. DrawMBar clips to the bar, erases its rounded top and draws the separator line. DrawMenuBar draws titles directly and uses GrayTitle or InvertTitle as needed. Removed the later menu-bar definition procedure and color tables."
    },
    {
      "kind": "title_hiliting",
      "description": "Restored GetNInvert and InvertTitle, with a title rectangle extending one pixel left and four pixels right. HiliteMenu inverts the old title and the requested title. FlashMenuBar saves its clip region, directly inverts a title or the whole bar, and restores the clip. The whole-bar path retains its fixed twenty-pixel height."
    },
    {
      "kind": "selection",
      "description": "Restored the forty-byte MenuSelect frame and direct menu-title hit testing. D3 holds the mouse point, D4 the previous menu-list index, D5 the current index and D6 the menu edge. A changed menu restores the old bits, checks dirty dimensions, positions the menu rectangle and calls MBarHook. The selection loop calls the menu definition, waits for mouse release, reads the next mouse point and calls MenuHook."
    },
    {
      "kind": "saved_bits",
      "description": "Restored inline bitmap allocation and CopyBits calls in DrawTheMenu. The saved rectangle includes the border and shadow but excludes the menu bar. Allocation failure records the rectangle in SaveRect; RestoreBits then asks PaintBehind to redraw it through a temporary region. A successful allocation uses SavedHandle and the local bitmap. Removed later multi-menu save stacks and definition-procedure wrappers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition_calls",
      "description": "Restored GetTheMProc, UnlockMProc and UnlkMDef. GetTheMProc loads the definition resource, directly sets its handle lock bit and returns its pointer. The unlock helpers directly clear that bit. CalcMenuSize pushes the size message and twelve bytes of unused parameters. CallChoose retains its busy wait against Ticks instead of the later Delay trap."
    },
    {
      "kind": "item_access",
      "description": "Retained the compact item-record search and shared property access paths. Restored the older register and stack layouts for MenuKey and menu-bar operations. Removed hierarchical searches, system-menu partitions, color records, script-manager calls and later parameter checks."
    },
    {
      "kind": "item_parser",
      "description": "Restored the original byte loop in AddString from instructions retained as comments in the later source. The ROM uses the original 280-byte item frame and seven-character syntax table. Four item-property bytes follow each string. The source preserves the table declarations, including the quoted semicolon, and removes the later hierarchical escape character and multibyte parser."
    },
    {
      "kind": "item_edits",
      "description": "Retained shared InsertTheItem, Munger calls, item-property copying, enable-bit rotations and DirtyMenuSize calls. Removed later checks for item numbers above 31 and the later nil-pointer guards. CountMItems retains its repeated GetItemRecord search, including the original comment about its cost."
    },
    {
      "kind": "resource_names",
      "description": "Restored InsrtResMenu after the AddResMenu wrapper. It saves ResLoad, disables automatic resource loading, enumerates names, skips empty names and names beginning with a period or percent sign, and inserts names in sorted order without duplicates. The comparison uses trap $A050, named RelString in the interface. FONT requests first enumerate FOND, then FONT; direct FOND requests also continue with FONT. It restores ResLoad after recalculating the menu size."
    },
    {
      "kind": "icon",
      "description": "Retained PlotIcon through the end of the module. It constructs a 32-by-32 monochrome bitmap in IconBitmap and calls CopyBits into the current port."
    },
    {
      "kind": "assembly",
      "description": "Made branch widths, instruction sizes and PC addressing explicit where needed to reproduce the ROM. Restored low-memory, menu-field and stack-frame equates, and bound Window Manager helpers to their ROM addresses. Trap calls remain named OPWORD declarations. Only the two character tables use data directives; no instruction is a raw byte stub."
    }
  ],
