      "address": "0x412a44",
      "description": "AddString enters the byte-processing loop before its first DBRA check. A zero-length string therefore does not take an early exit. The reconstruction retains this behavior."
    },
    {
      "address": "0x412404",
      "description": "EnableItem and DisableItem pass the supplied item number directly to a register bit operation. The 68000 uses its low five bits; the later greater-than-31 guard is absent."
